   "about": "A compiled digest summarizes July 1943 reports on production, finance, food supply, infrastructure, administrative transfers and communications across Japan and territories under Japanese control.",
   "summary": "The document continues an already-begun numbered series, opening with the end of an item about Sugitani's vehicle-maintenance research and proceeding through reports numbered 17–101; only the heading for item 102 appears at the end. Its regional sections cover Japan, Manchuria, Inner Mongolia, occupied North China, occupied Central and South China, Hong Kong and the Philippines. Reports emphasize strategic-resource production, agricultural and industrial controls, economic cooperation with the Nanking regime, the return of concessions and controlled property, and the restoration or expansion of postal, telegraph, shipping and banking services. Most reports are credited to Domei in English, Japanese or Chinese, with others attributed to Nanking's Central News Agency and Peiping's Chunghua News Agency.",
